<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?><ns2:section xmlns:ns2="http://rest.cis.illinois.edu" id="63498" href="schedule/2021/spring/GLBL/296/63498.xml"><parents><calendarYear id="2021" href="schedule/2021.xml">2021</calendarYear><term id="120211" href="schedule/2021/spring.xml">Spring 2021</term><subject id="GLBL" href="schedule/2021/spring/GLBL.xml">Global Studies</subject><course id="296" href="schedule/2021/spring/GLBL/296.xml">Global St Foundation Seminar</course></parents><sectionNumber>H  </sectionNumber><sectionTitle>Comm, Identity Global Kenya</sectionTitle><sectionDateRange>Meets 25-Jan-21 - 19-Mar-21.</sectionDateRange><statusCode>A</statusCode><sectionText>The course examines the impact of economic globalization on the community and identity formations in Africa with special reference to the multicultural, multilingual East African country of Kenya. The patterns of maintenance and shift of identities of various ethnic groups, including the Indians, will be examined to evaluate co-existence of a large number of transnational corporations with the growing forces of ethno-nationalism.    This course will be synchronous ONL sessions via Zoom.</sectionText><partOfTerm>A</partOfTerm><sectionStatusCode>A</sectionStatusCode><enrollmentStatus>UNKNOWN</enrollmentStatus><startDate>2021-01-25Z</startDate><endDate>2021-03-19Z</endDate><meetings><meeting id="0"><type code="ONL">Online</type><start>07:00 PM</start><end>08:50 PM</end><daysOfTheWeek>T      </daysOfTheWeek><meetingDateRange>Meets 25-Jan-21 - 19-Mar-21.</meetingDateRange><instructors><instructor lastName="Gathogo" firstName="M">Gathogo, M</instructor><instructor lastName="Mishra" firstName="M">Mishra, M</instructor></instructors></meeting></meetings></ns2:section>